#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133582 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133773 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "77b63ba5-410b-536c-8ed0-92c895097cc9" :question/math-academy-id "e-5554" :question/problem "Consider the vector ![](images/d1/d1a095e61e6ea64f97a105fd69bc07f3f44990cd6d9794e54e355463c37a2413.png) Given that $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=-12$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v}\\Vert =4,$ what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n\\vert \\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\vert \\leq \\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert.$ So first, we compute $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-12| & \\le \\sqrt{6+k}\\cdot (4) \\\\ 12 & \\le 4\\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ 3 & \\le \\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ {3}^{2} & \\le (\\sqrt{6+k})^{2} \\\\ 9 & \\le 6+k \\\\ 3 & \\le k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133583 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "763f7e8e-081a-57ad-825f-601a38fe3984" :question/math-academy-id "e-5555" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vectors ![](images/5e/5ed21f4bb536757026315cce838f4cc3028493adac2ff29d46a5b8cbdf11170b.png) and ![](images/8d/8d813e104a708be37ba44b9448806f49ea21a16fe7f613314d2eeab2b59bbda2.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert \\, \\Vert \\mathbf{w}\\Vert},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta=\\arccos \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right)=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133631 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "0562751a-55be-5fd1-83d2-11795ba7a052" :question/math-academy-id "e-5910" :question/problem "Let $A(-2, 4, -2, 2)$ and $B(4, 0, -1, -4).$ Find the cosine of the angle $\\angle{AOB},$ where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}$ be the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}.$ Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133773 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077df59b-1576-5984-a140-c65b2aede902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269338} {:answer/id #uuid "2d0c0613-1639-5681-9e9b-c1c15e1ba0aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269671} {:answer/id #uuid "542362db-81d4-5fad-9cea-4f106d534926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270019} {:answer/id #uuid "f04d156a-1e93-57a2-9459-aab8a017e33b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271382} {:answer/id #uuid "f814c357-1424-5c62-90b6-9762bfa07488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "542362db-81d4-5fad-9cea-4f106d534926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270019} :answer-field/id #uuid "e78a8507-0510-559f-a33b-04cce5d3f0f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd33e455-0f47-57d5-9add-73b07f36d75e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140440" :question/problem "Given that $‖u‖=5$ and $u\\cdot v=-15$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-15| & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 15 & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 15 & \\le \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$\nis  $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133773 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4b40e7-7e79-5dc6-9f22-f4558da9b9c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269395} {:answer/id #uuid "682e849a-558d-5162-8470-48b8b0d005c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270193} {:answer/id #uuid "94b67a9f-2b85-5e2a-b0f9-f8cd57845deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270573} {:answer/id #uuid "d99ea119-fcf0-55dc-9a31-11cd4e526b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271176} {:answer/id #uuid "fa07f8c6-53a8-57c0-b460-7c9e2cc0539c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d99ea119-fcf0-55dc-9a31-11cd4e526b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271176} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc1c0671-653c-5406-ae27-4391da28d55b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a38c7df6-58f3-5ed8-95a4-2f7e4b402435" :question/math-academy-id "q-140442" :question/problem "Consider the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} \\\\ -\\sqrt{k} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u\\cdot v=-2$ and $‖v‖=1$, what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n|u\\cdot v|\\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $‖u‖.$ So first, we compute $‖u‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+2k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-2| & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k}\\cdot (1) \\\\ 2 & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k} \\\\ {2}^{2} & \\le {(\\sqrt{2+2k})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & \\le 2+2k \\\\ 2 & \\le 2k \\\\ k & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6634a7a3-3929-507a-be37-d16878113fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270178} {:answer/id #uuid "9d870ff5-d1b6-5d0e-8114-886ea90c0cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270663} {:answer/id #uuid "cf91ab12-8782-58a2-b350-ec2395222e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271088} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb3b8bf-93a9-578e-ba9d-16f1d5dc8c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271089} {:answer/id #uuid "d836fdb8-f279-5f91-b2fd-7b0ab72f31bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{22}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6634a7a3-3929-507a-be37-d16878113fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270178} :answer-field/id #uuid "411aef24-61e3-5692-9c0c-aa1c7d631569" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae7334f7-ce11-500e-b881-3d819bbe315f" :question/math-academy-id "q-140455" :question/problem "Let $A(1,0,-1,2)$ and $B(4,8,2,-2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+0\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{88}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133773 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa8f571-e93d-536e-a93f-00454d982b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131348} {:answer/id #uuid "f071e5f0-622b-5413-afd5-cbdf6bcbfe3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131349} {:answer/id #uuid "1616527e-5593-5f69-9da2-4346fcca3765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131350} {:answer/id #uuid "2576db8d-85e2-524f-9908-6d6c1c4ee0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131351} {:answer/id #uuid "7304e2ee-df74-53ba-979d-daa9a2498ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131352}] :answer-field/id #uuid "460e4a56-c5b3-5c60-8042-f665921b5b45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131347}] :question/id #uuid "29218d0d-65a8-5002-8e66-efb867e9e6d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-39432" :question/problem "