on "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{7})+7\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{7})^{2}+{7}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{7})^{2}+{3}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{64}\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d88320-9c11-5280-b76f-40d6819c8636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82.34}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324026} {:answer/id #uuid "283eced6-cba8-5ab9-873f-cef502a919af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70.76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324294} {:answer/id #uuid "6620172a-f34f-54bf-b674-5f04d8ca274e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324821} {:answer/id #uuid "78b6dccb-d580-5fdc-8de6-f8a96aed4746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{72.25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324975} {:answer/id #uuid "9db5ec7a-7db2-58bf-963a-dfc9df68138a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{89.76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283eced6-cba8-5ab9-873f-cef502a919af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70.76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324294} :answer-field/id #uuid "68ef84f4-2d5d-528b-a1d0-77a23ef63f01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca41f5b8-b3cf-55a5-b73c-3a463b4f4955" :question/math-academy-id "q-40566" :question/problem "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors  $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\text{ }1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot (-5)+5\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{67}\\sqrt{55}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}})≈{70.76}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133773 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b08080b-ea84-5f2f-9038-8fbbb8663140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324068} {:answer/id #uuid "0ffd0a9a-74a1-52c9-b9aa-afcbf5ab14ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324120} {:answer/id #uuid "710a1e51-91c7-5c9c-91e0-1e7bdf05caa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324903} {:answer/id #uuid "ee68afbe-64af-55e0-ba58-5742dc5c6b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326073} {:answer/id #uuid "f65254cf-2099-5b56-ba02-d5213f6cdc58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee68afbe-64af-55e0-ba58-5742dc5c6b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326073} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dff11e7-f6e4-56ef-bacf-474584363b92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ea0a813-a7a6-50d9-bc45-5213ad249e0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40882" :question/problem "Consider the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u\\cdot v=-20$ and $‖v‖=5$,  what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n|u\\cdot v|\\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $‖u‖.$ So first, we compute $‖u‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-20| & \\le \\sqrt{14+k}\\cdot (5) \\\\ 4 & \\le \\sqrt{14+k} \\\\ {4}^{2} & \\le {(\\sqrt{14+k})}^{2} \\\\ 16 & \\le 14+k \\\\ 2 & \\le k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16764aae-eac9-5050-95ab-08a340a76923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339327} {:answer/id #uuid "63b5e09c-27f2-5e98-b1b9-0e3d6b6dbd12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340013} {:answer/id #uuid "84e0cbc3-1cde-5f0e-81b4-39906c424c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340322} {:answer/id #uuid "8a684e5a-cce0-5074-908c-a046797de1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340365} {:answer/id #uuid "a793d995-cf50-57e6-9168-520c43507e64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84e0cbc3-1cde-5f0e-81b4-39906c424c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340322} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec060fc7-478c-5567-872b-98da99a7f890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d38c4f2-4cfd-5f2e-9ed7-b5d4ad5c5c7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74105" :question/problem "Let $A(1,-3,2,-1)$ and $B(1,1,3,-2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{15}\\cdot \\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{6÷3}{15÷3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1280d778-2b40-5f2f-a030-8629b0402012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339289} {:answer/id #uuid "14f7da9d-88ee-58af-9b13-d197483dc16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339314} {:answer/id #uuid "313a11cb-009a-5b5f-bc41-94ecbd447c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339562} {:answer/id #uuid "61467cd7-ca79-5de8-816b-a2b182f506d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339995} {:answer/id #uuid "c61ab2bb-9649-5028-9423-f2a1f2240208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "313a11cb-009a-5b5f-bc41-94ecbd447c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339562} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e5df36-07a6-50c3-a7e9-01c8c7409c5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b674ce78-18bf-5ff8-a526-99d8937fa2a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74110" :question/problem "Let $A(0,-2,1,-3)$ and $B(-1,2,2,-3).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot (-3)}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{18}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
